https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EU-CTPc5GJg  (Capo 1) (MC2)

The opening bit is a series of individual strums like this:  three downstrokes and one up stroke of (Em), then on the next downstroke lift off the top finger so only note <e> is fretted, and finish with an upstroke of (Em).  So it goes down-down-down-up-DOWN-up with you lifting off the top finger on the last down.  Yes there’s a cadence to this sequence but don’t overthink it.  Just listen to the opening a few times.  The whole sequence is played 3 times followed by a lead in with the (Em).

TIP:  The song ends with 9 single strums of (Em), the first coming on the last word of the song.  


